NEARS-1084/1088 QA — pre-existing a11y defect on the CATEGORY screen error state
(NEARS-596 surface; NOT introduced by Sprint-5 Batch-3).

The NearsErrorRetry state on category_screen.dart:420 collapses into ONE merged
semantics node covering the entire screen. The Retry button is not individually
focusable/announceable, and any label-driven tap resolves the node's centre —
which is the cloud ICON, not the button.

uiautomator dump (verbatim):

node index="0" text="" resource-id="" class="android.view.View"
  package="com.izzes.nears"
  content-desc="Something went wrong&#10;Please check your connection and try again&#10;Retry"
  checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="true" enabled="true"
  focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false"
  password="false" selected="false" bounds="[0,0][1344,2920]" drawing-order="0"

Impact: a screen-reader user hears the whole screen as a single blob and cannot
target Retry; automated label-driven taps land on dead space.

Contrast: the SAME widget on store_screen.dart exposes `Retry` as its own node
and taps correctly. So this is a category-screen tree/merge issue, not a
NearsErrorRetry / NearsEmptyState defect.

Repro: Categories tab -> any category -> fail /api/v1/categories/items/<id>
-> dump the a11y tree.
